## Imported musl material

Wlibc is planned to use musl as its initial implementation base. Any musl
source imported in the future must retain the upstream copyright and license
notices. The musl project states that musl as a whole is MIT-licensed, while
some files and bundled components carry their own notices or license terms.

Before importing a pinned musl revision, Wlibc must:
- record the exact upstream commit and source archive hash;
- preserve the upstream COPYRIGHT file in the source distribution;
- preserve file-level notices and all applicable third-party license texts;
- inventory optional components and exclude any component not approved for Wicofe;
- record local modifications and their rationale; and
- produce a machine-readable and human-readable third-party inventory.

No musl source import or completed provenance audit is claimed by this
architecture-only repository state.

